EXPLAIN: the developer's primary tool
Every database has EXPLAIN. It shows the query plan. Most are terrible. Postgres's EXPLAIN ANALYZE is the gold standard despite being verbose; pgvector's EXPLAIN is essentially useless (it shows "Bitmap Index Scan on vector_idx" with no useful information about HNSW behavior).
For us, EXPLAIN matters more than usual because our planner makes multi-modal decisions users will second-guess. "Why did it pre-filter instead of using HNSW?" needs an answer the user can verify.
EXPLAIN modes:
EXPLAIN <query>: shows the physical plan with cost estimates. No execution.
EXPLAIN ANALYZE <query>: executes the query, shows the plan with actual statistics alongside estimates.
EXPLAIN VERBOSE <query>: includes everything — column projections, expressions, cost breakdowns, statistics references.
EXPLAIN (FORMAT JSON) <query>: machine-readable output for tooling.
