Distributed tracing
For requests that span multiple operations (a transaction with multiple queries, a query that calls external embedding API), tracing connects the dots.
OpenTelemetry as the standard. We instrument:

Query lifecycle (parse, plan, execute) as a span
Each major operator execution as a child span
External API calls (embedding services) as child spans
I/O operations (page reads, compactions) as child spans (sampled, not all)

Output: OTel spans exported to whatever backend the user configures (Jaeger, Tempo, Datadog, Honeycomb, etc.).
Sampling: 100% sampling is too expensive for production. We default to 1% sampling of normal queries, 100% sampling of slow queries (>1s) and errors. Configurable.
Trace context propagation: the gRPC interceptor reads OTel headers from incoming requests, attaches to outgoing requests (to embedding APIs etc.). This lets users trace from their application all the way through us to external services.
